title: Building, web pages, and grammar
card: Chapter 11 | Building | A program of its own
say:
  So far Fathom has run our programs directly. But a program can also be built: made into a dot exe file that runs on its own, and fast, on any Windows computer, without Fathom.
uncard

new: count.fathom
type:
  genesis:
    set total to 0
    for each n from 1 to 1000000:
      set total to total plus n
    scrawl "One to a million adds up to ", total with commas
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-5
say: Here's a program that adds up every number from one to a million.
zoom: out
build
zoom: output
say:
  Build turns it into C++, and then into a program of its own. Built programs run far faster, so they're the way to go for games.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 11 | Web pages | Programs inside a page
say:
  The Web button makes a program into JavaScript instead, so it can be the inside of a web page, or an app.
  The page library gives it the page.
uncard
new: clicker.fathom
type:
  use: page

  the world remembers:
    clicks (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to pressed, given event (a number):
    set clicks to clicks plus 1
    set the text with (the element "#count", "Clicks: " plus clicks)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    listen for an event with (the element "button", "click", the command pressed)
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 12-14
spot: line 13
say:
  Listen for an event says: when the button on the page is clicked, do the command pressed.
  The element button finds it, the same way CSS selectors do.
spot: off
zoom: lines 7-10
spot: line 8
say: Pressed counts the click.
spot: line 9
say: And set the text puts the count into the element whose id is count.
spot: off
zoom: out
web
zoom: output
say:
  It made clicker dot j s, and Fathom's own runtime next to it. A page that loads them both runs the program.
  This studia is made this way: its screens are written in Fathom, and so is the part that reads and writes your files.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 11 | WebAssembly | Machine code that runs anywhere
say:
  There's one more way. WebAssembly is machine code that isn't for any one kind of computer, so the same file runs on Windows, Mac and Linux, and in browsers and servers.
uncard
open: count.fathom
wasm
zoom: output
say:
  The Wasm button builds the same machine code as an exe, but as WebAssembly: count dot wasm. Node, or any WebAssembly runner, runs it, with node count dot m j s.
  It can read and write files, ask, and do everything the language itself does. Windows' own libraries, like windows and sound, don't work there yet.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 11 | Grammar for people | Reading like English
say:
  Fathom is written for people to read. So in a few places, it asks for grammar, even though the computer skips it.
uncard
new: grammar.fathom
type:
  a notice has:
    title (text)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    conjure a notice as first notice
    set the title of first notice to "Hello"
    set shown notices to a list containing first notice
    scrawl size of shown notices
  and the universe said i love you
run: expect a mistake
zoom: output
say:
  Write the size of, not size of. The is needed before a part of something: the size of, the title of.
wait
zoom: out
line: 9
keys: backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace
type: the size of shown notices
zoom: lines 6-9
spot: line 6
say: A or an is needed after conjure. And it checks you wrote a before a consonant, and an before a vowel.
spot: line 8
say: And a is needed before list containing.
spot: off
say:
  Everywhere else, the, a and an are up to you. Set the notices, and set notices, are the same line.
  That's also why a, an and the can't be names on their own.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out
